.TH VMREAD 1 8/29/91
.CM 4
.SH NAME
vmread \- read a task's address space (specifically with 8086 style output).
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBvmread\fP pid [addr] [size] [offset]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fIvmread(1)\fR reads and displays a task's address space.
The \fIpid\fP argument, a unix server pid, specifies the task.
The \fIaddr\fP argument is a hexadecimal number
specifying the starting address.  This number may be
an absolute address, or an 8086 style address using a colon
to separate the segment and the offset.
The \fIsize\fP argument is a hexadecimal number
specifying the number of bytes of memory to read.
.PP
\fIvmread\fR displays the memory using ASCII, sixteen bytes per line.
.PP
You must either be root or the task's owner to gain access to the
target task.
.PP
.SH "SEE ALSO"
ps(1), vmdis(1)
